WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.570
In this video, you will find the neighborhood contests, where you can vote for your favorite homes, enter your own, or see who won.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:08.656
We start on the map.

00:00:09.562 --> 00:00:11.311
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:12.913 --> 00:00:15.431
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.147
Then tap Allow.

00:00:22.132 --> 00:00:24.821
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:24.821 --> 00:00:26.017
See the three dots?

00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:30.319
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:30.319 --> 00:00:30.857
Tap them.

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:34.276
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.039
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:44.681
Live now lists the contests that are open today.

00:00:44.681 --> 00:00:49.185
On each one, you can vote for your favorite homes, or enter your own home.

00:00:49.185 --> 00:00:54.710
Voting and entering each have their own dates, so a contest shows what you can do right now.

00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:56.534
Tap Mine.

00:00:58.446 --> 00:01:00.023
This is your personal page.

00:01:00.023 --> 00:01:05.208
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:06.114 --> 00:01:08.695
Tap Past results, for contests that are finished.

00:01:10.449 --> 00:01:14.438
You can see the winners in every category, and look back at earlier years.

00:01:15.343 --> 00:01:19.379
That is the Contests page: Live now, Mine, and Past results.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:27.716
Contests also show up on the map as cards, with a button to enter or vote, so you may find one without ever opening this page.

00:01:29.126 --> 00:01:32.027
Next up: Find professionally installed displays.
